{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'tail -n 3 docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md'","aggregated_output":"| 39 | 11-05 | 第 3 步：做进正式系统（设计四张表，Codex 审 3 轮：第 1 轮 4 条严重、第 2 轮 2 条严重，都改；第 3 轮无严重问题） | 建成 `baseline.run` + poc-v116 + baseline-v3 提示词文件；$0 核对：44 份请求和验证时逐字节相同，3 次存下的回答走正式代码写出的记录完全一样，第一天判断正好判这些题，网页从开始跟踪那天可见；新测试 12 条、6 个弄坏版本都抓出、全套 272 条通过；设计页和 PRD 00/03/04/05/06 更新，`docs/check.py` 通过 | 交 Alex：要不要跑 14 天三遍完整验收（约 5 美元） |\n| 40 | 11-05 | Alex：\"跑验收\"。14 天三遍完整验收：poc-v116（开始跟踪时读财报）三遍、当天重跑 poc-v108 三遍作对照，冻结尺子打分（事先锁定 `acceptance-design.md`）；电脑中途在电池上睡了约 5 小时，6 遍被暂停，插电后自己接着跑完 | **全过**：v10、v12 各 3/3（对照从没判过）；合计 53 对 45（满分 57，+8）；唯一少两次的 v17（0/3 对 2/3）两人都认定不是起点数：同一份抽取请求，新配置两遍碰巧留下\"中国份额归零\"那句，对照没留；约 4.79 美元 | 交 Alex：poc-v116 是否成为默认 |\n| 41 | 11-05 | Alex：\"都做\"（poc-v116 设成默认；提交代码、开 PR）。默认配置改成 poc-v116，默认的条目数据库换成带财报网页原文的那一份（旧的没有原文，新默认会在它上面拒跑）；测试按用户的用法补上：不给种子题就拒绝，给了就先读财报再跑第一天 | 测试全过，5 个弄坏的版本都抓出；配置的设置和验收三遍记下的校验码一致（只改了配置里的注释）；花钱前的检查脚本在新配置的运行数据上照常跑完，但不复查读财报那一步的引用检查（记为未补的缺口）；D366 | 提交、开 PR；下一类问题等 Alex |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '1,155p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# \"Forecast unavailable\" release: build design for slice 1 (the exporter and the checked package)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Status: revision 7, for council round 74g. No code yet.** Release work was opened by the council under D439 (D758). The behaviour is\n     4\tfixed by D726, D756 and `FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4). This page holds the AGENTS §2 tables for the first slice.\n     5\t\n     6\t**Revision 2 answers `codex-r74.md`** (see `claude-r74.md`):\n     7\t- the pass condition is an origin check of every field against its stored source, not a string sweep;\n     8\t- a missing source item is refused;\n     9\t- the package is checked before it is moved into place;\n    10\t- the manifest is a closed set;\n    11\t- the bound is validated as a date;\n    12\t- narrow reads;\n    13\t- size and speed budgets;\n    14\t- tests that separate every branch;\n    15\t- `object`, `kind` and groups dropped;\n    16\t- no idea submission.\n    17\t\n    18\tThe evidence summary stays as extraction stored it (§8, disputed in `claude-r74.md`).\n    19\t\n    20\t**Revision 3 answers `codex-r74b.md`.**\n    21\t- The checker derives everything it compares from the store, never from the package: the date, each question's class, the records and their counts.\n    22\t- A missing source item refuses `check` too.\n    23\t- The files must be two regular, non-symlink files, with no duplicate JSON member names.\n    24\t- The staging folder has one owner.\n    25\t- The builder's refusal is tested through the builder.\n    26\t- The diagnostics read only the columns a store has.\n    27\t\n    28\t**Revision 4 answers `codex-r74c.md`.**\n    29\t- One date rule for build and `check`.\n    30\t- Questions are ordered by `created_seq, rowid`.\n    31\t- (Superseded in revision 5.) The build claimed its output folder before staging.\n    32\t- Cleanup sits where the staging path is known.\n    33\t- A report failure after publication has its own outcome.\n    34\t- The builder's refusal is proved through the real command on a scratch copy.\n    35\t- Tests 9, 13, 14 and 15 are sharpened.\n    36\t\n    37\t**Revision 5 answers `codex-r74d.md` with one structural rule** (AGENTS §1: the publication mechanism drew findings in 74b, 74c and\n    38\t74d). Staging is private, and the only public step is one atomic move that refuses any existing destination. There is no public\n    39\tclaim, so nothing public is created early or cleaned up. Staging is removed in a `finally` covering its whole life, so any error,\n    40\tdatabase errors included, leaves nothing at `--out`.\n    41\t\n    42\t**Revision 6 answers `codex-r74e.md`.**\n    43\t- The build's cleanup responsibility ends the moment `publish` succeeds: the staging path is cleared and the `finally` removes nothing\n    44\t  after that, so a folder later created at the freed staging name is never touched.\n    45\t- The late refusal at `publish`, and the end of cleanup after it, are proved through the real command on scratch copies with a\n    46\t  pause.\n    47\t\n    48\t**Revision 7 answers `codex-r74f.md`.**\n    49\t- An explicit day is parsed first and used everywhere in its canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` form. Python reads `20260825` as the same day,\n    50\t  but the stores compare days as text.\n    51\t- Neither command writes a report over an input database.\n    52\t\n    53\t## 0. Scope\n    54\t\n    55\t- **Slice 1 (this page), $0:**\n    56\t  - the exporter `release_export` and its self-check;\n    57\t  - the package writer, the package check and the origin check;\n    58\t  - the release builder, which calls the exporter directly;\n    59\t  - tests and mutants;\n    60\t  - the $0 release check on stored stores.\n    61\t- **Slice 2, next.** The release page reads only the package: no live service, no `/library` fetch, no translated JSON, no composite\n    62\t  trials, no idea submission control or route. It gets a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen, which completes D756's screen check.\n    63\t- **No idea submission in the release** (council 74). The idea path (`idea.py`) reads the ledger at every step and calls a paid model\n    64\t  per idea. The design's §5 idea acceptance (an idea card backed only by `v8`, and its composed request) is carried forward as pending\n    65\t  for the first idea-enabled slice.\n    66\t- **Not in scope:**\n    67\t  - the POC, its API, MCP and page (unchanged);\n    68\t  - colleagues' page;\n    69\t  - frozen pieces, extraction included;\n    70\t  - any model call;\n    71\t  - commit, publish, deploy.\n    72\t\n    73\t## 1. What is built\n    74\t\n    75\t`src/hivemind/release.py` is the one owner, beside `service.py`.\n    76\t\n    77\t- **Constants:**\n    78\t  - `FORMAT = 'hivemind-release/1'`;\n    79\t  - `ALLOW_LIST = 'release-allow-list/1'`;\n    80\t  - `FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE = 'Forecast unavailable'`;\n    81\t  - `PACKAGE_FILES = {'manifest.json', 'release-data.json'}`.\n    82\t- **`ALLOWED`:** the closed key set per record type.\n    83\t\n    84\t  | Record | Keys |\n    85\t  |---|---|\n    86\t  | envelope | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `questions` |\n    87\t  | number question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (= `number`), `forecast` (= the marker), `evidence` |\n    88\t  | event or Yes/No question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (`event` or `yes_no`), `answers` (the two stored rung labels, in position order), `answer` (the stored label of the latest judgement's rung on or before the bound, or null), `evidence` |\n    89\t  | evidence in force at the bound | `id`, `one_line`, `quote`, `tier`, `speaker`, `original_who`, `original_day`, `sources` |\n    90\t  | source recorded on or before the bound | `title`, `publisher`, `day`, `uri` |\n    91\t  | manifest | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `data_sha256` |\n    92\t\n    93\t- **`question_class(views_db, view_id, labels)`** (design §3):\n    94\t  - `event` when the view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES`. The key is read as `select measure from view_keys`, and\n    95\t    only when the table exists;\n    96\t  - `yes_no` when there are exactly two labels which, through `vocabulary.canonical('label', …)`, are `Yes` and `No` in either order;\n    97\t  - `number` otherwise: a view with no key, or one whose bands cannot be resolved.\n    98\t- **`release_export(views_db, items_db, as_of=None)`:**\n    99\t  - pins both connections (`bundle.read_snapshot`);\n   100\t  - takes an explicit day only in canonical form: `date.fromisoformat(day).isoformat()` must equal the text given, otherwise\n   101\t    `ReleaseRefused` (so `20260825` is refused, not read as `2026-08-25`). It then resolves the bound with `service.resolve_bound`,\n   102\t    refuses a store with no default day, and uses that canonical text in every query;\n   103\t  - exports every view that exists at the bound (`service.view_exists`), closed ones included, in `created_seq, rowid` order;\n   104\t  - builds each record field by field from the table above, with column-limited SQL:\n   105\t    - `select view_id, question, created_seq from views order by created_seq, rowid`;\n   106\t    - `select position, label from rungs`;\n   107\t    - `select rung from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1`;\n   108\t    - `service.is_open_as_of`, which reads only `open` and `after_seq`;\n   109\t  - takes evidence in force from `service.evidence` and its fields from that record;\n   110\t  - looks up each source's `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri` in the items database by `input_id`. A visible source whose item is\n   111\t    missing raises `ReleaseRefused` (there is no fallback to the id);\n   112\t  - calls `check_export` on its own result before returning (AGENTS §3: the writer refuses).\n   113\t- **`check_export(data)`:** the closed-set check.\n   114\t  - Every dict at every level has exactly its record type's keys.\n   115\t  - Value checks:\n   116\t    - `format` and `allow_list` equal the constants, and `as_of` is a canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` day (`date.fromisoformat(as_of).isoformat() == as_of`);\n   117\t    - `class` is in its set;\n   118\t    - a number record's `forecast` is the marker;\n   119\t    - `answers` is two strings, and `answer` is one of them or null;\n   120\t    - `open` is a bool and every text field is a string.\n   121\t  - It returns the counts it judged: questions per class, evidence, sources.\n   122\t- **`check_origins(views_db, items_db, data, expected_as_of)`:** the pass condition. It is independent of the exporter's code path.\n   123\t  It derives everything it compares from the store, never from the package.\n   124\t  - **The bound: one rule for both commands.** `expected_as_of` is given by the caller.\n   125\t    - The builder passes the bound it resolved: `service.resolve_bound` on the requested day, or the default when none is given; an\n   126\t      omitted day with no default is refused.\n   127\t    - `check` passes the package's `as_of` through the same `service.resolve_bound`, which refuses a day after a store's last\n   128\t      completed day. A legacy ledger with no completed days accepts any valid date in both commands alike.\n   129\t    - The package's `as_of` must equal `expected_as_of`.\n   130\t  - **The class** of each question is derived from the stored measure and labels (`question_class`). The permitted keys and values\n   131\t    are then chosen from that class, never from the package's `class` field.\n   132\t  - **Order and counts.** The questions are compared as an ordered list in `created_seq, rowid` order, as `bundle.library` orders\n   133\t    them (`old-2/v2` and `v3` share sequence 8). Each question's evidence is compared in link order (`evidence_links.id`), and its\n   134\t    sources in row order (`evidence_sources.id`). A duplicate question, evidence record or source therefore fails.\n   135\t\n   136\t  It compares every field with its permitted stored source at the bound, by direct SQL:\n   137\t  - the question set equals the views visible at the bound, with `question` equal to `views.question`;\n   138\t  - `open` equals the latest visible switch's `open`;\n   139\t  - for `event` and `yes_no`: `answers` equal the rung labels in position order, and `answer` equals the label of the latest judgement\n   140\t    rung on or before the bound, or null;\n   141\t  - for `number`: only the marker;\n   142\t  - the evidence id set equals the links visible at the bound, minus those whose latest replacement is visible, computed in its own\n   143\t    SQL. Each evidence field equals the `evidence` row's column;\n   144\t  - each source list starts from every visible `evidence_sources` row, in row order, with `day` taken from\n   145\t    `evidence_sources.publication_day`. Each row needs a matching `items` row for `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri`; a row with no\n   146\t    item raises `ReleaseRefused` (a left join, so a missing item is never silently dropped).\n   147\t\n   148\t  Any difference raises `ReleaseRefused`, naming the question, the field and the evidence id. It returns the number of fields\n   149\t  compared.\n   150\t- **`stage(out_dir)`:** creates a private staging folder with a name unique to this invocation, `tempfile.mkdtemp(dir=out_dir.parent,\n   151\t  prefix='.<name>.staging-')`. Creation is exclusive, so only this invocation owns it. It returns the path.\n   152\t- **`write_package(data, staged)`:** writes `release-data.json` and `manifest.json` into the staging folder. It creates nothing\n   153\t  else.\n   154\t- **`publish(staged, out_dir)`:** one atomic move that refuses any existing destination, empty or not:\n   155\t  - on macOS, `renamex_np(staged, out_dir, RENAME_EXCL)` through `ctypes`. Verified on this Mac: onto a free path it succeeds; onto\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '301,445p'\"","aggregated_output":"   301\t1. **Closed set (§1).**\n   302\t   - Every dict in a fixture export has exactly its type's keys.\n   303\t   - Positive control: an export with one added key fails `check_export`.\n   304\t2. **Number with `lo`/`hi`.** The record carries the marker. No rung label, condition, `reasons`, `why_changed` or `implied_outcome` of\n   305\t   that view appears in any decoded package field.\n   306\t3. **Branch fixtures for identity and the report:**\n   307\t   - a condition-only number that resolves: `number`, and absent from `withheld_unresolved`;\n   308\t   - an unresolved number with a key: `number`, and present;\n   309\t   - an unresolved number without a key: `number`, and present.\n   310\t4. **Yes/No with numeric bounds** (`growth_rate` key, labels Yes/No): `yes_no`, with its answer label. A `why_changed` quoting\n   311\t   \"$1 trillion\" is absent.\n   312\t5. **Event with the served ledger's `v49` labels,** \"Restriction adopted\" / \"No restriction adopted\": `event`, with its label kept. A\n   313\t   `why_changed` quoting another question's band is absent.\n   314\t6. **Legacy store** with no `view_keys` table and `是`/`否` labels: `yes_no`.\n   315\t7. **Closing switch** whose reason names the band label: `open: false`, and the reason is absent.\n   316\t8. **Replacement and source visibility** at two bounds. A visible source with a missing item is refused.\n   317\t9. **Package:**\n   318\t   - staged, then checked, passes;\n   319\t   - a foreign file fails, and so does a subdirectory;\n   320\t   - a changed data byte fails;\n   321\t   - an extra manifest key with an unchanged data hash fails;\n   322\t   - a manifest `as_of` differing from the data's fails;\n   323\t   - an existing `--out`, empty or not, is refused, and a leftover staging folder from another build does not block a build.\n   324\t10. **Origin check, each from the store:**\n   325\t    - in a staged copy, the system's forecast text placed in an evidence `one_line` fails, naming the field;\n   326\t    - a Yes/No record turned into a number record, keeping the closed set, fails;\n   327\t    - a duplicated question, and a duplicated evidence record, each fails;\n   328\t    - a package whose `as_of` is a day later than the store's last completed day fails `check`;\n   329\t    - a legacy fixture with no completed days, built at an explicit day later than its last judgement, passes a later `check`.\n   330\t11. **Builder end to end,** run as the user calls it (subprocess, `--as-of` omitted). The package is final and passes `check`.\n   331\t12. **Builder refusal, through the real command, on a scratch copy** (the AGENTS §4 mutation procedure; no fake in the suite):\n   332\t    - the unchanged command succeeds on the fixture store (test 11);\n   333\t    - on a scratch copy, the writer fault \"one evidence `one_line` taken from the latest judgement's `why_changed`\" is introduced.\n   334\t      The same command exits 1 with the origin-mismatch reason, no `--out` and no staging folder left;\n   335\t    - on a second scratch copy, the same writer fault plus the builder's staged check removed: the bad package reaches `--out`. That\n   336\t      shows the staged check is what prevents publication.\n   337\t13. **`check` with a missing item.** A finished package. Then a copy of the items database with one referenced item deleted, and a\n   338\t    copy of the package with that same source removed and its manifest hash refreshed. `check` refuses, naming the missing item. (An\n   339\t    inner-join mutant accepts this pair, so this case catches it.)\n   340\t14. **The publication rule.**\n   341\t    - Module steps: builds A and B both stage, then A publishes. B's `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`. A's package passes `check`, and\n   342\t      B's staging is still there for its owner to remove.\n   343\t    - Module steps: after staging, a foreign *empty* folder is put at `--out`. `publish` refuses, and the foreign folder still exists\n   344\t      afterwards, empty.\n   345\t    - The command, early: an existing empty `--out` gives exit 1, and the folder survives.\n   346\t    - The command, late (a scratch copy with a pause before `publish`, released by the test): the test creates an empty folder at\n   347\t      `--out` during the pause. The command exits 1, its staging folder is removed, and the same empty folder survives (same device\n   348\t      and inode).\n   349\t    - The command, after the move (a scratch copy with a pause just after `publish`): the test recreates the freed staging name as a\n   350\t      folder holding a marker file. After the command exits 0, the marker is still there.\n   351\t18. **Report over an input.** `--out` chosen so that `<out>.report.json` is the items database (a symbolic link to it, and the same\n   352\t    path): `build` refuses, and so does `check` on an existing package. The items file's sha256 is unchanged.\n   353\t17. **A database error through the command.** A valid ledger with an items database that has no `items` table: exit 1, the database\n   354\t    error printed, nothing at `--out`, no staging folder left. A retry at the same `--out` with the correct items database succeeds.\n   355\t15. **Files:**\n   356\t    - a symbolic link in place of `release-data.json` fails;\n   357\t    - a data file whose repeated `one_line` member has the genuine value last, with the manifest hash refreshed so every other\n   358\t      check passes, fails on the repeated name.\n   359\t16. **Bound validation:**\n   360\t    - `2026-08-99` is refused;\n   361\t    - `20260825` is refused, while `2026-08-25` builds. On a fixture with evidence on both sides of that day, the package holds only\n   362\t      the earlier evidence;\n   363\t    - a valid day before the first question gives an empty package.\n   364\t\n   365\t**Mutants,** on a scratch copy with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; each must fail a test:\n   366\t- `condition` emitted on number records;\n   367\t- `one_line` taken from the latest judgement's `why_changed`;\n   368\t- the event test removed;\n   369\t- the Yes/No test removed;\n   370\t- `check_package` without the file-set check;\n   371\t- manifest keys unchecked;\n   372\t- `check_export` without the closed-key check;\n   373\t- `check_origins` skipping evidence fields;\n   374\t- `check_origins` taking the class from the package;\n   375\t- `check_origins` comparing sets instead of ordered lists;\n   376\t- `check_origins` with an inner join to `items`;\n   377\t- `check` without validating the package's `as_of` against the store;\n   378\t- the builder skipping the staged `check_package` (the scratch-copy pair in test 12);\n   379\t- `publish` replaced by `os.rename` (test 14's foreign empty folder is then replaced);\n   380\t- the `finally` removed (test 17 then leaves staging);\n   381\t- the staging path not dropped after `publish` (test 14's marker is then removed);\n   382\t- the canonical-day check removed (test 16's `20260825` then builds with later evidence);\n   383\t- the report-path collision check removed (test 18's items file is then overwritten);\n   384\t- the symbolic-link check removed;\n   385\t- the duplicate-key check removed;\n   386\t- the switch reason emitted;\n   387\t- the missing-item refusal replaced by the id fallback.\n   388\t\n   389\t## 7. The $0 release check (stored stores, read-only)\n   390\t\n   391\tStores: `old-1`, `old-2`, `old-3` (`comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-N/prod/views.sqlite`, items `items-comparison.sqlite`) and the\n   392\tserved ledger with its items database.\n   393\t\n   394\t**Budgets,** set before the first control (AGENTS §2):\n   395\t- the package's data bytes at most `bundle.library`'s JSON bytes on the same store and bound;\n   396\t- export plus all checks at most three times `bundle.library`'s seconds on the same store, and at most 120 s per store.\n   397\t\n   398\tThe steps:\n   399\t1. **Build each store's package at its default bound.** The build passes `check_package` with `check_origins`. Report the fields\n   400\t   compared, the counts per class and the unresolved list.\n   401\t2. **The decisive acceptance case** (council 74), on the `old-1` package:\n   402\t   - Morningstar's `$361 billion` estimate (`e2295`) is kept, its summary and quote equal to the stored ones;\n   403\t   - the genuine \"Bullish confirmation\" quote (`e1865`) is kept;\n   404\t   - the genuine analyst \"$390 billion\" quote (`e3597`) is kept, as the control;\n   405\t   - in a copy of the staged package, the system's `old-1` j1580 `implied_outcome` (\"About $390 billion…\") substituted into\n   406\t     `e2295`'s summary fails `check_origins`;\n   407\t   - the same text added to the manifest fails `check_package`.\n   408\t3. **`old-1/v8`:** `class` is `number`, with the marker and the same evidence ids as `service.evidence` at the bound.\n   409\t4. **The known event leaks at their own dates.** Export `old-3` at 2026-08-25 (`v36` j799 is the latest judgement) and `old-1` at\n   410\t   2026-08-28 (`v10` j865). Each keeps its original answer label, and j799's \"around $1 trillion\" text and j865's band text are absent.\n   411\t5. **Control:** one unchanged event question keeps its label and evidence.\n   412\t6. **Closing.** On a temporary copy of `old-1`, add a closing switch for `v8` in the store's own format (\"due …, frozen on … at\n   413\t   rung N <label>\"). First confirm that `bundle.view_bundle` exposes the reason with the band label. Then confirm the package shows\n   414\t   `open: false` and not the reason.\n   415\t7. **Diagnostics** (not the gate). For every question, take each string the package must not hold:\n   416\t   - rung labels and conditions;\n   417\t   - judgement `reasons` and `why_changed`, and `implied_outcome` and `reference` where the store has those columns (the served\n   418\t     ledger has neither; the report says so);\n   419\t   - switch reasons.\n   420\t\n   421\t   Search every decoded string field of the package for each, with no floor. List every hit with its question, field, evidence id\n   422\t   and the stored string it matched, and read each by hand. A genuine source quote, such as `e1865`'s \"Bullish\", is recorded as such.\n   423\t8. **Budgets:** bytes and seconds against the budgets above.\n   424\t\n   425\t## 8. A disclosed property, not built: evidence summaries keep extraction's wording\n   426\t\n   427\tThe release shows each evidence summary as extraction stored it; the release computes or converts nothing. A summary can make\n   428\tcontext explicit or restate a source figure by arithmetic, attributed to its source: `old-1/e3238` gives \"more than $40 billion in\n   429\tFY2028\" for a quote's \"more than double that next year\".\n   430\t- **Measured:** 25.6%, 25.2% and 25.4% of evidence in force in `old-1`, `old-2` and `old-3`, and 35.0% in the served ledger, carry a\n   431\t  number not in their quote. In a sample of 24, 23 are context: a year, a date, a quarter, a product name, an amount from the previous\n   432\t  sentence. One restates \"close to doubling\" as \"nearly 100%\".\n   433\t- **Why this is not the forecast D726 withholds.** Extraction never sees the system's forecast. Its request lists each open question\n   434\t  only as id, object, due day, question and a \"takes\" line (`placement.py:19-61`, `extraction.py:398-400`); no rung, label or\n   435\t  judged position.\n   436\t- **Council 74b** (`codex-r74b.md` §2) verified that extraction sends no rung, label or judged position, and that the census\n   437\t  reproduces.\n   438\t- **The disagreement that remains is narrow.**\n   439\t  - Codex reads revision 4's \"amounts as quoted\" as requiring source wording for a calculated amount attributed to a source, such\n   440\t    as `e3238`'s \"more than $40 billion\".\n   441\t  - Claude reads it as \"the release computes or converts nothing\".\n   442\t  - Both agree: no digit filter, no change to extraction.\n   443\t- **The course taken.** By AGENTS' rule for an unsettled disagreement, the cheaper, reversible course is to keep the stored summary.\n   444\t  The quote is shown beside it, so the source wording is on the reader's screen. A later version can drop the field from the\n   445\t  allow-list or change it.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '156,300p'\"","aggregated_output":"   156\t    an existing empty or non-empty folder it fails with `EEXIST`, and both folders stay as they were;\n   157\t  - on Linux, `renameat2(AT_FDCWD, staged, AT_FDCWD, out_dir, RENAME_NOREPLACE)`;\n   158\t  - where neither call exists, or the filesystem lacks support (`ENOTSUP`, `EINVAL`), it raises `ReleaseRefused`.\n   159\t\n   160\t  It never replaces, creates or removes anything at `out_dir` except by that one move.\n   161\t- **`check_package(path, views_db=None, items_db=None, expected_as_of=None)`:**\n   162\t  - the directory holds exactly `PACKAGE_FILES`, each a regular file and not a symbolic link (`os.lstat`), with no subdirectories;\n   163\t  - both files parse as JSON with no duplicate member name at any level (an `object_pairs_hook` that refuses a repeated key);\n   164\t  - the manifest has exactly its four keys, and its `format`, `allow_list` and `as_of` equal the data's;\n   165\t  - its sha256 equals the data file's;\n   166\t  - the data passes `check_export`, and, when the stores are given, `check_origins` with the expected bound;\n   167\t  - it returns the counts.\n   168\t- **`withheld_unresolved(views_db, data)`** is for the report only. It lists the number questions whose `service.ladder_bands(rungs)`\n   169\t  returns `(None, reason)`, with the reason and whether the view has a key. Its output never enters the package.\n   170\t\n   171\t`scripts/release_build.py`:\n   172\t- **`build --ledger --items [--as-of] --out`:**\n   173\t  1. refuse an existing `--out` early, as a convenience; `publish` holds the guarantee. Refuse when `<out>.report.json` exists, or\n   174\t     when it, or `--out`, resolves (`os.path.realpath`) to the ledger or items path;\n   175\t  2. resolve the bound once: a given `--as-of` must be canonical `YYYY-MM-DD` (as above), then `service.resolve_bound`;\n   176\t  3. `stage(--out)`. From here a `finally` removes this staging folder while the build still owns it;\n   177\t  4. `release_export` at that bound;\n   178\t  5. `write_package` into the staging folder;\n   179\t  6. `check_package` on the staged folder, with the stores and the resolved bound;\n   180\t  7. `publish` to `--out`. The moment it succeeds, the build drops its staging path (`staged = None`); the `finally` then removes\n   181\t     nothing;\n   182\t  8. write `<out>.report.json` beside the package, through a temporary file and `os.replace`.\n   183\t\n   184\t  The failure outcomes:\n   185\t  - **Before publication** (steps 2–7): any exception, whether `ReleaseRefused`, `OSError`, `sqlite3.Error` or another, prints the\n   186\t    reason and exits 1. The `finally` removes this build's staging folder; nothing exists at `--out` from this build. A corrected\n   187\t    retry at the same `--out` succeeds.\n   188\t  - **After publication** (step 8 fails): the package is final and checked. Exit 2 with \"package published and checked; report not\n   189\t    written; run `check` to regenerate it\".\n   190\t\n   191\t  It has no input path for prepared or translated JSON, and it takes no clock reading; the folder name is the caller's (D12, D13).\n   192\t- **`check <out> --ledger --items`:** first refuses when `<out>.report.json` resolves (`os.path.realpath`) to the ledger or items path.\n   193\t  It then re-runs `check_package` on an existing package, with the stores, the package's canonical `as_of` validated against the store\n   194\t  (above), and the regular-file and duplicate-key checks. It leaves the package in place and rewrites\n   195\t  `<out>.report.json`. This is also the retry after a report write failed. Its report gives `check_seconds` and marks\n   196\t  `export_seconds` as not measured.\n   197\t- **The report:**\n   198\t  - the store path and the bound;\n   199\t  - counts per class;\n   200\t  - the unresolved list;\n   201\t  - the fields compared;\n   202\t  - bytes;\n   203\t  - `export_seconds` (build only) and `check_seconds`.\n   204\t\n   205\t## 2. State × event (one export, read-only)\n   206\t\n   207\t| State / event | What happens | What is written | Day used |\n   208\t|---|---|---|---|\n   209\t| Store's first day still in progress | `FirstDayNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | none |\n   210\t| Store with no completed day and no judgement, `--as-of` omitted | refused: \"no default day; supply --as-of\" | nothing | none |\n   211\t| `--as-of` not a valid date (`2026-08-99`) | refused by `date.fromisoformat` | nothing | none |\n   212\t| `--as-of` valid but not canonical (`20260825`) | refused: the stores compare days as text, so a non-canonical day would read rows from later days | nothing | none |\n   213\t| The report path resolves to the ledger or items input (build or `check`) | refused before anything is read or written; the input's bytes are untouched | nothing | — |\n   214\t| `--as-of` after the last completed day | `BoundNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | requested day |\n   215\t| `--as-of` valid, before the first visible question | empty `questions`; the report says 0 | package | bound |\n   216\t| `--as-of` omitted | last completed day (a legacy ledger: its last judgement day) | package | resolved bound |\n   217\t| View created after the bound | not exported | — | bound |\n   218\t| View closed on or before the bound | `open: false`, with no reason and no day | — | bound |\n   219\t| Closed, then reopened, before the bound | the last visible switch wins | — | bound |\n   220\t| Event or Yes/No not yet judged at the bound | `answer: null` | — | bound |\n   221\t| Evidence replaced on or before the bound | excluded; the replacement is in force | — | bound |\n   222\t| Evidence replaced after the bound | kept | — | bound |\n   223\t| Source recorded after the bound | excluded | — | bound |\n   224\t| Visible source with no row in the items database | `ReleaseRefused`, naming the evidence and input id | nothing final | bound |\n   225\t| Store written by a live run | not supported. The builder is given a snapshot (AGENTS §9), and both connections are pinned | — | — |\n   226\t| `--out` exists, empty or not, at the start | refused early; `publish` would also refuse | nothing | — |\n   227\t| `check_export`, `check_package` or `check_origins` refuses | this build's staging folder is removed, exit non-zero | nothing final | — |\n   228\t| A write, check or move fails, or a database error (`sqlite3.Error`, such as an items database with no `items` table) | exit 1; the `finally` removes this build's staging; a corrected retry at the same `--out` succeeds | nothing | — |\n   229\t| A folder, empty or not, appears at `--out` after staging | `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`; that folder is untouched; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing of this build | — |\n   230\t| The filesystem has no atomic no-replace move | `publish` refuses; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing | — |\n   231\t| Crash while staging | a uniquely named staging folder is left as debris. Nothing is at `--out`, and no later build is blocked | staging only | — |\n   232\t| Crash after the rename, before the report | the package is final and checked; `check` rewrites the report | package | — |\n   233\t| The report write fails after publication | exit 2: the package is final and checked; `check` regenerates the report | package | — |\n   234\t| Two builds aimed at one `--out` | each stages privately; the first `publish` wins; the second's `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`, and its `finally` removes only its own staging | the winner's package | — |\n   235\t| Package `as_of` later than the store's last completed day (`check`) | refused by `resolve_bound` | nothing | package `as_of` |\n   236\t| A legacy ledger with no completed days, explicit day | the build and `check` both accept any valid date (one rule) | package | requested day |\n   237\t| A package file is a symbolic link, or a JSON member name repeats | `check_package` refuses | nothing | — |\n   238\t| The package's `class` disagrees with the store's (a Yes/No answer replaced by the marker) | `check_origins` refuses: class is derived from the store | nothing final | bound |\n   239\t| Store or configuration changed between builds | each package records its bound and data sha256; the report names the store path | — | — |\n   240\t| Legacy ledger: no `view_keys` table, `是`/`否` labels | no key, so no event; the labels canonicalise to Yes/No | — | — |\n   241\t\n   242\t## 3. Value × reader\n   243\t\n   244\tReaders of the package:\n   245\t- `check_package` and `check_origins`;\n   246\t- the release page (slice 2);\n   247\t- the tests.\n   248\t\n   249\tThe report's reader is the person building. No POC code imports `release`.\n   250\t\n   251\t| Value | Permitted source at the bound | Checked by |\n   252\t|---|---|---|\n   253\t| `id`, `question` | `views.view_id`, `views.question` | `check_origins` |\n   254\t| `open` | the latest visible `view_switches.open` | `check_origins` |\n   255\t| `class` | `view_keys.measure`, `rungs.label` | `check_origins` derives it from the store; tests and mutants check the identity rule |\n   256\t| `answers`, `answer` | `rungs.label` by position; the latest `judgements.rung` on or before the bound | `check_origins` |\n   257\t| `forecast` | the constant marker | `check_export` |\n   258\t| evidence fields | the `evidence` row; visible `evidence_links` minus visible replacements | `check_origins` |\n   259\t| source fields | every visible `evidence_sources` row (`publication_day` as `day`); its `items` row's `title`, `publisher`, `source_uri`, required | `check_origins` (left join; a missing item refuses) |\n   260\t| manifest | the data's `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`; the data sha256 | `check_package` |\n   261\t| report (outside the package) | `ladder_bands` per number question; counts | read by the builder's user |\n   262\t\n   263\t**Never read by `release_export`:**\n   264\t- `rungs.condition`, `lo`, `hi`;\n   265\t- `judgements.reasons`, `why_changed`, `implied_outcome`, `reference`, `pushes_json`, `theme_pushes_json`, `cited_*`;\n   266\t- `view_switches.reason`;\n   267\t- `clean_ladders`;\n   268\t- `thesis_groups`;\n   269\t- `dependencies`, `successions`.\n   270\t\n   271\t## 4. New path × old checks\n   272\t\n   273\t| Check on the old path (`bundle.library`, `view_bundle`, `service`) | New path |\n   274\t|---|---|\n   275\t| `resolve_bound`: unfinished first day, future bound | same call |\n   276\t| `bundle.library`: no default day refused; `date.fromisoformat` | same two checks |\n   277\t| A view not visible at the bound is not served | same `view_exists` |\n   278\t| Sources visible at the bound; replacements applied | same `service.evidence`, verified independently by `check_origins` |\n   279\t| Pinned read transaction | same `bundle.read_snapshot` |\n   280\t| `item_lookup` falls back to the id for a missing item | refused instead |\n   281\t| A malformed `clean_ladders` row is refused | not read |\n   282\t| Corrupt judgement JSON is refused | no JSON column read |\n   283\t| The UI contract rejects unknown fields | the release's own `check_export`; the page's reading of it is slice 2 |\n   284\t\n   285\t## 5. Prior decisions\n   286\t\n   287\t- D726: number questions show sources and \"Forecast unavailable\", with band, forecast text and history withheld together.\n   288\t- D756: Alex's choice.\n   289\t- D757: the design, revision 4.\n   290\t- D758: the release is opened; §4 (a); order.\n   291\t- D12/D13: no clock.\n   292\t- D163: English product text.\n   293\t- D690: poc-v118 stays the product.\n   294\t- D261: the ruler is untouched.\n   295\t- D274: the extraction prompt is frozen.\n   296\t\n   297\t## 6. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\n   298\t\n   299\tThe fixtures use a real store on a temporary path (`store.create_view`, `store.insert`), with a real items database. Each test names\n   300\tits row above:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
