{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'report.*(exist|replace|overwrite)|existing report|report path|report.*after' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/{RELEASE-BUILD.md,codex-r74*.md}\"","aggregated_output":"docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74f.md:1:**Not ready to build.** Revision 6 closes both 74e findings. Two other issues remain. A package dated August 25 can include September evidence, and writing the report can overwrite an input database.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74f.md:11:- **The report can replace the ledger or items database.** For example, with `--out /work/release` and a valid SQLite input named `/work/release.report.json`, the build can read the input, verify and publish the package, then replace that database with JSON. The standalone `check` command rewrites the same path. Both commands should refuse a report destination that resolves to either input before writing anything. The decisive test is that each command refuses the collision and the input’s bytes remain intact. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:166](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:166) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:175](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:175) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:185](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:185)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74c.md:22:- **Put cleanup where the staging path is known, and distinguish failure after publication.** If either file write fails, `write_package` has created staging but has yet to return its path to the caller. It must clean up there, or the caller must acquire staging before the writes. After a successful rename, a report-write error has the opposite outcome: the checked package exists and `check` can regenerate its report. The blanket “no final folder exists” rule gives the wrong recovery action at that point. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:120](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:120) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:145](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:145) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:150](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:150)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:33:- A report failure after publication has its own outcome.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:173:  1. refuse an existing `--out` early, as a convenience; `publish` holds the guarantee. Refuse when `<out>.report.json` exists, or\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:182:  8. write `<out>.report.json` beside the package, through a temporary file and `os.replace`.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:195:  `<out>.report.json`. This is also the retry after a report write failed. Its report gives `check_seconds` and marks\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:213:| The report path resolves to the ledger or items input (build or `check`) | refused before anything is read or written; the input's bytes are untouched | nothing | — |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:233:| The report write fails after publication | exit 2: the package is final and checked; `check` regenerates the report | package | — |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"agent_message","text":"**Not ready to build.** Revision 7 closes the date finding. Two ways to overwrite a file remain in the report-writing steps.\n\n1. **74f date finding — closed.** The builder rejects `20260825` before querying the ledger. The package checker also requires `YYYY-MM-DD`. Test 16 places evidence on both sides of August 25 and checks that the canonical date exports only the earlier evidence. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:100](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:100) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:116](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:116) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:359](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:359)\n\n2. **74f input-overwrite finding — still open in `check`.** On this Mac, I verified read-only that `old-1/prod/views.sqlite` and `old-1/prod/VIEWS.SQLITE` produce different `realpath` strings and identify the same file. An items database named `Release.report.json` can therefore pass the path comparison for `check release`, which then rewrites `release.report.json`. Compare the existing report’s file identity with both inputs using `os.path.samefile`. Extend test 18 on a case-insensitive volume to require refusal and an unchanged database hash. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:192](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:192) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:351](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:351) · [live_lock.py:40](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/live_lock.py:40)\n\n3. **Additional blocker — `build` can overwrite a file created while it runs.** The builder checks that the report name is free at startup. If another process creates a file there while the package is being checked, the final `os.replace` overwrites it. Publish the build’s report with an atomic operation that refuses an occupied destination. The decisive test places a marker file there immediately before the report write and requires the marker to survive, the checked package to remain available, and the command to exit 2. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:173](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:173) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:182](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:182) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:188](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:188)\n\nI found no further serious blocker in slice 1."}}
